      "name": "ru-allowed",
      "preamble": "# ru-allowed — accepted words that never fire\n\n**Status:** v2, 2026-10-08. This file is the source of truth; edit it directly.\n\nSame pattern syntax as `ru-non-approved` (`стем:n`, `стем:v`, `[пре]стем`, exact word).\n\nClasses:\n- `latin` — a Latin word that may stand in prose without backticks. It never fires `latin-prose`. Case is ignored.\n- `loanword` — a standard Russian IT loanword. If a token or a hyphen part matches, no lexicon row fires on it.\n- `glued` — a Latin acronym + hyphen + Russian noun that Russian orthography accepts. Only listed compounds pass the `glued` rule.\n\nGlued decision: `CI-` compounds are never allowed. «CI-матрица» is banned, so «CI-пайплайн», «CI-нога» and «CI-сервис» fire too. Write «пайплайн CI», «матрица CI». Acronyms that name a protocol or a format (HTTP, gRPC, SQL, JSON, API, FIFO) may glue to a short generic noun listed below.\n\n| term | class | note |\n|---|---|---|\n",
